  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-10T11:47:30.769Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The latest development update says that the intent going forward is to eventually reduce the number of updates down to one a week.\nThis makes sense given no development studio is seriously going to tell its users literally every thing that happened every day, and the curation time is very long.\nHowever, the last time there was supposed to be a \"regular\" series of posts, it dried up really quickly.\nAs an alternative to going to a once-a-week schedule:\n1. Keep the twice-a-week schedule that is starting on the week commencing 15/08/2022\n2. Change one of the two updates to being a 'community' post, covering things like cool new worlds/avatars and upcoming events, and allow it to be a \"catch up\" if the development update is late.\nTwo posts a week, one being less critical than the other, means something can go wrong without losing too much cadence, and it'd be an opportunity for VRChat to post \"hey look at this cool new world\" or whatever without having to stick it on Spotlight.",
